  {"step":2,"desc":"stand P and turn it nine turns alone — then stand Q downstream of it, and wake both","dige":"909b8be07deddf61"}
  step=3,desc:11 clock pulses each — the pair woken along its wires,dige:742e391161c638dc
    Assertion:a-stream-carries-nothing,sentence:a stream carries nothing while the fish upstream are young — the tank downstream holds only its own
  step=4,desc:one clock pulse each — the pair woken along its wires,dige:dc3ad6c315beb52e
    Assertion:a-fish-too-old,sentence:a fish too old for one tank swims down the stream into the next — one pulse each — and is gone from the first
    Assertion:a-fish-keeps-its,sentence:a fish keeps its age crossing to a tank on another clock — born on that clock before its first turn
  step=5,desc:one clock pulse each — the pair woken along its wires,dige:cc20706aea836779
    Assertion:the-old-fish-leave,sentence:the old fish leave the tank downstream on its next turn — while its own oldest are far younger
